From: sdolbec <sdolbec1@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: thunderbolt: describe optional Apple DP source

Opt-in experimental source bridge; apply after 0001 through 0006.
Prepare DCP outside the TB lock before any DPRX read. Match source
ownership and asynchronous cancellation to the tunnel lifetime.
Adopt discovered host tunnels and keep domain references until destroy.
See DCP-SOURCE-BRIDGE.md for validation and qualification limits.

Signed-off-by: sdolbec <sdolbec1@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thunderbolt/apple,t8103-usb4-nhi.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thunderbolt/apple,t8103-usb4-nhi.yaml
index a80c8db..e6c8eaf 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thunderbolt/apple,t8103-usb4-nhi.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thunderbolt/apple,t8103-usb4-nhi.yaml
@@ -90,6 +90,19 @@ properties:
       T6030, T6031 and T8122 use 24 IOMMUs. These are most likely one DART
       stream for each of the 12 transmit and 12 receive rings.
 
+  apple,dp-source:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description: |
+      Experimental display controller feeding the host DP-IN adapter selected
+      by apple,dp-in-port. Its phys must reference an enabled DP-IN provider
+      under the same ACIO parent. Omit both properties for the normal NHI path.
+
+  apple,dp-in-port:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+    minimum: 1
+    maximum: 255
+    description: Explicit host-router DP-IN adapter number for apple,dp-source
+
   apple,thunderbolt-drom:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint8-array
     description:
@@ -116,6 +129,10 @@ required:
   - iommus
   - apple,thunderbolt-drom
 
+dependentRequired:
+  apple,dp-source: ['apple,dp-in-port']
+  apple,dp-in-port: ['apple,dp-source']
+
 allOf:
   - if:
       properties:
